# CWC technical constraints

This repo is the **Flutter** cross-platform (Android + iOS) build under Dr. Haghani / ECE students.

## Platform

- **Android-first:** optimize for budget / government-program devices; include a low-RAM (~2GB) device in the test matrix; Android 8+ era baseline.
- **Ship platforms: Android + iOS only.** Do not add or revive Flutter web for this study build (not in CI; `web/` removed).
- Installed size target **&lt; ~40MB**; no mandatory large first-run downloads.
- Videos and map tiles: Wi‑Fi or explicit user action only.
- Prefer open-source / low-cost dependencies (TECH-8).

## Offline-first

Every MVP feature except optional map tiles and external links must work **with no connectivity**. Bundle/cache: Nearby list, Learn, tutorials metadata, Help Now numbers. Sync content opportunistically when online via remote-config / hosted JSON (no app-store release for content-only updates).

## Privacy & security (study build)

- Personal health data **local-only**; encrypt at rest (platform Keystore / Keychain via secure storage).
- No ads, no third-party analytics SDKs, no location tracking.
- If user opts into GPS for Nearby: use coordinates **transiently on-device** for distance; never store/transmit.
- PIN/biometric may protect My Health only—never Nearby, Learn, tutorials, or Help Now.
- One-tap erase personal data; hide My Health from app-switcher previews while that tab is open (Android `FLAG_SECURE`).
- Usability instrumentation only behind a research build flag + consent disclosure.

## Accessibility

- WCAG 2.1 AA; ≥48dp targets; never color-only meaning.
- Base body **≥18pt** + in-app larger-text toggle; honor OS font scaling.
- Icons always paired with text labels; TalkBack + VoiceOver; no gesture-only actions.

## Before shipping Help Now

Verify NJ peer warmline number/hours with CSPNJ; CAB-approve the resource set.
